===Verb===
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{en-past of|gild}}

===Adjective===
{{head|en|adjective}}

# Having the color or quality of [[gold]].
# Made of gold or covered by a thin layer of gold.
# Having a falsely pleasant appearance; [[sugarcoat]]ed.
#* '''1596-97''', [[w:William Shakespeare|William Shakespeare]], ''[[w:The Merchant of Venice|The Merchant of Venice]]'', Act II Scene 7
#*: All that [[glister]]s is not gold;
#*: Often have you heard that told:
#*: Many a man his life hath sold
#*: But my outside to [[behold]]:
#*: '''Gilded''' tombs do worms [[infold]].
#*: Had you been as wise as bold,
#*: Young in limbs, in judgement old,
#*: Your answer had not been inscroll'd:
#*: [[fare|Fare]] you well; your [[suit]] is cold.

